From 3fd1db24dc51b028945cbe78b32c54977bd6e95c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:33:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Verifier V26: the custody sends' walk with V23's SendCaravan
 rules [skip ci]

On c260c438 (V23's route, check_caravan, check_slots made crate-visible
by workstream 4): DepositLot, ShipLot and WithdrawLot are judged as
proc::custody's `send`, which is SendCaravan's: the fee at least the
caravan fee, the first path Province the origin's (its public
address), V23's walk and schedule over the path Provinces before it
with the Citizen's faction and the Season's stances (Walker::of), the
tower wear, each run's slot written (check_slots), the Caravan as
written (check_caravan: owner, number, faction, origin, destination,
the sent cargo worn, fee, departure, arrival, last slot bell), and the
Citizen's caravan counter moved by one.

A send whose lot side, records and walk all match is now a full match;
a deposit from a holding stays UNVERIFIABLE (its debit is V7's). A
state the walk needs and the input lacks (the Season, a path Province
before or after, the source, the Citizen after) leaves the route not
judged: UNVERIFIABLE with the reason, never PASS, never a default.
SettleCustody's Province conditions, fee and rent stay UNVERIFIABLE.

Tests (no key generated, derived or used to sign): a ShipLot inside one
Province whose walk writes a slot, a full match; the arrival a second
late, the slot not written, the counter not moved, a path that misses
the destination, a fee below the caravan fee, a first Province that is
not the origin's: FAIL; the Season, a Province before or after, the
Citizen after missing: not judged. The caravan test fixtures now carry a
valid fee and the Province at its address.

